# Task 0l — warning[3000] false-positive pin set (the `(a)` valid-Z98 families).
#
# Contract: after Task 0m, each directory below MUST produce ZERO
# `warning[3000]` diagnostics from the compiler under test. Check with:
#
#   bash scripts/corpus/w3000_census.sh <zig1> repro/mi_matrix/w3000_fp_pins.list
#
# This is the pin mechanism the gcc-based classifier cannot provide: a Z98
# `warning[3000]` is tolerated (the program still compiles and runs), so it never
# changes the gcc exit code.
#
# The 11 `(b)` invalid-Zig dirs are intentionally NOT here (Task 0q promotes
# them to hard `error[3000]`, a different contract).
# `repro/field_store_tagged` is NOT here: Task 0l found its `source: type` is the
# diagnostics-string fallback for `usize`, and the warning is a REAL
# `usize -> u32` same-width mismatch (see task-0l-report.md). Declared, not pinned.

